{
 "id": "l41",
 "label": "41",
 "title": "Formation of adjectives",
 "summary": "Turning root words into describing words with ma-, ka-, kay-, maka-, pang-/pam-/pan-, mapag- and pala-",
 "minutes": 35,
 "goals": [
  "Use ma- + root for having a quality (magandá) or having plenty of something (mabulaklák)",
  "Use ka- for a shared relationship (kabalát) and kay- for exclamations (kaygandá!)",
  "Use maka- for being in favor of someone or something (makabágo)",
  "Choose pang-, pam- or pan- to show what something is used for",
  "Use mapag- and pala- to describe what someone does habitually"
 ],
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "Making describing words",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "Many Tagalog adjectives (describing words) are built from a **root word** plus a **prefix** (a piece added to the front). Each prefix gives the new word a particular kind of meaning. This lesson goes through the prefixes the book lists, one group at a time."
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "head": [
      "Prefix",
      "What the new word means",
      "Example"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "[[ma-|pred]] (abstract root)",
       "having the quality of the root",
       "[[magandá|pred]]  beautiful"
      ],
      [
       "[[ma-|pred]] (concrete root)",
       "having many or much of the root",
       "[[mabulaklák|pred]]  many flowers"
      ],
      [
       "[[ka-|pred]]",
       "a reciprocal (shared) relationship",
       "[[kabalát|pred]]  of the same skin"
      ],
      [
       "[[kay-|pred]]",
       "an exclamation: *how …!*",
       "[[kaygandá|pred]]  how beautiful!"
      ],
      [
       "[[maka-|pred]]",
       "in favor of someone or something",
       "[[makabágo|pred]]  modern"
      ],
      [
       "[[pang-|pred]], [[pam-|pred]], [[pan-|pred]]",
       "for a specific use",
       "[[pambáyad|pred]]  for payment"
      ],
      [
       "[[mapag-|pred]], [[pala-|pred]]",
       "does something habitually or frequently",
       "[[palatawá|pred]]  laughs frequently"
      ]
     ],
     "title": "The adjective prefixes at a glance"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Ma-: having a quality",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "**Ma- + root** means *having the quality* expressed by the root. Use it with **abstract nouns**: things you cannot touch, such as beauty or knowledge. (You met this idea with **may** in Lesson 12: the book shows each ma- word as the same as **may** + the root.)"
    },
    {
     "type": "pattern",
     "title": "ma- + abstract root",
     "rows": [
      {
       "label": "Root",
       "chips": [
        {
         "t": "gandá",
         "r": "noun"
        },
        {
         "t": "beauty",
         "r": "other"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "label": "Adjective",
       "chips": [
        {
         "t": "ma-",
         "r": "pred"
        },
        {
         "t": "gandá",
         "r": "noun"
        },
        {
         "t": "→ magandá",
         "r": "pred"
        }
       ]
      }
     ],
     "note": "magandá = beautiful (may ganda)"
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "head": [
      "Root",
      "Adjective"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "[[gandá|noun]]  beauty",
       "[[magandá|pred]]  beautiful (may ganda)"
      ],
      [
       "[[baít|noun]]  goodness",
       "[[mabaít|pred]]  good (may bait)"
      ],
      [
       "[[tamís|noun]]  sweetness",
       "[[matamís|pred]]  sweet (may tamis)"
      ],
      [
       "[[dúnong|noun]]  knowledge",
       "[[marúnong|pred]]  learned (may dunong)"
      ]
     ],
     "title": "Ma- with abstract nouns"
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "rule",
     "title": "D changes to R",
     "t": "Look at the last one. When **ma-** is added, a root that starts with **d** changes that **d** to **r**: ma- + **d**únong becomes ma**r**únong."
    },
    {
     "type": "vocab",
     "group": "ma1",
     "title": "Ma-: having a quality"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Ma-: having plenty",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "With **concrete nouns** (things you can see and touch), **ma- + root** means having *many* or *much* of the thing named by the root."
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "head": [
      "Root",
      "Adjective"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "[[bulaklák|noun]]  flower",
       "[[mabulaklák|pred]]  many flowers"
      ],
      [
       "[[táo|noun]]  person",
       "[[matáo|pred]]  many people"
      ],
      [
       "[[bigás|noun]]  rice",
       "[[mabigás|pred]]  plenty of rice"
      ],
      [
       "[[búnga|noun]]  fruit",
       "[[mabúnga|pred]]  plenty of fruits or fruitful"
      ]
     ],
     "title": "Ma- with concrete nouns"
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "tip",
     "title": "Abstract or concrete?",
     "items": [
      "Abstract root (beauty, sweetness): ma- gives the **quality**. Magandá = beautiful.",
      "Concrete root (flower, rice): ma- gives **plenty of** it. Mabigás = plenty of rice."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "vocab",
     "group": "ma2",
     "title": "Ma-: having plenty"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Ka- and kay-",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "h",
     "t": "Ka-: a shared relationship"
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "**Ka- + root** refers to a **reciprocal relationship**: something that two people share or do together."
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "head": [
      "Root",
      "Adjective"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "[[balát|noun]]  skin",
       "[[kabalát|pred]]  of the same skin"
      ],
      [
       "[[sama|pred]]  to go along",
       "[[kasama|pred]]  accompanied"
      ]
     ],
     "title": "Ka-"
    },
    {
     "type": "h",
     "t": "Kay-: how …!"
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "**Kay- + root** makes an **exclamation** about the trait named by the root. Kay- literally translates to *how*."
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "head": [
      "Root",
      "Exclamation"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "[[gandá|noun]]  beauty",
       "[[kaygandá|pred]]  how beautiful!"
      ],
      [
       "[[ága|noun]]  early",
       "[[kay-ága|pred]]  how early!"
      ],
      [
       "[[buti|noun]]  goodness",
       "[[kaybúti|pred]]  how good!"
      ]
     ],
     "title": "Kay-"
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "english",
     "title": "Like English *how*",
     "t": "*How beautiful!* and *How early!* are exactly what kaygandá and kay-ága say. The whole exclamation is one Tagalog word."
    },
    {
     "type": "vocab",
     "group": "ka",
     "title": "Ka- and kay-"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Maka-: in favor of",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "**Maka- + root** means *in favor of someone over another*, or *inclined to believe in someone or something*. The root may even be a **proper name**."
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "head": [
      "Root",
      "Adjective"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "Rizal  Philippines' national hero",
       "[[maka-Rizal|pred]]  in favor of Rizal"
      ],
      [
       "[[bago|pred]]  new",
       "[[makabágo|pred]]  (in favor of new); modern"
      ],
      [
       "[[lumà|pred]]  old",
       "[[makalumà|pred]]  (in favor of old); old fashioned"
      ]
     ],
     "title": "Maka-"
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "tip",
     "title": "Read the literal meaning first",
     "t": "Makabágo is literally *in favor of the new*, which is why it means **modern**. Makalumà is *in favor of the old*, so it means **old fashioned**."
    },
    {
     "type": "vocab",
     "group": "maka",
     "title": "Maka-"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Pang-, pam- and pan-: what it is for",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "**Pang- + root** refers to the **specific use** expressed by the root: what something is *for*. The prefix changes its ending to suit the first letter of the root."
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "head": [
      "Prefix",
      "Use it when the root starts with",
      "Hyphen?"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "[[pang-|pred]]",
       "a vowel (a, e, i, o, u) or k, g, h, m, n, ng, w, y",
       "yes, before a vowel: pang-umága"
      ],
      [
       "[[pam-|pred]]",
       "b or p",
       "no"
      ],
      [
       "[[pan-|pred]]",
       "d, l, r, s or t",
       "no"
      ]
     ],
     "title": "Choosing the prefix"
    },
