  {
   "title": "Practise like the book",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "The book's own exercises ask you to (1) write five adjectives, using a variety of affixes, to describe **New York**, a **gurò** (teacher) and a **babáe** (woman), and (2) add **pang-**, **pam-** or **pan-** to these roots: bansâ, gámit, aral, bása, lahát, langóy, batà, kain, barò, ilaw."
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "tip",
     "title": "How to work them out",
     "t": "For the second exercise, look only at the **first letter** of each root and use the table in the pang- section: vowel or k, g, h, m, n, ng, w, y → pang- (with a hyphen before a vowel); b or p → pam-; d, l, r, s or t → pan-. The book does not print the answers, so check them with a teacher or a Tagalog speaker."
    }
   ]
