 "recap": [
  "Ma- + abstract root = having the quality (magandá, beautiful); ma- + concrete root = plenty of it (matáo, many people).",
  "With ma-, a first d becomes r: dúnong → marúnong.",
  "Ka- = shared relationship (kabalát); kay- = how …! (kaygandá, kay-ága, kaybúti).",
  "Maka- = in favor of: maka-Rizal, makabágo (modern), makalumà (old fashioned).",
  "Pang- / pam- (b, p) / pan- (d, l, r, s, t) = for a specific use: pambáyad, pantúlog, pang-umága.",
  "Mapag- and pala- = does it habitually (palatawá, mapag-arál); pala- only with action roots."
 ]
